{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Surādha","html":"<article id='thag2.8'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.8 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.8 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Paṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter One </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Surādhattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Surādha </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Khīṇā hi mayhaṁ jāti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Rebirth is ended for me; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vusitaṁ jinasāsanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the victor’s instruction is fulfilled; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pahīno jālasaṅkhāto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>what they call a “net” is given up; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhavanetti samūhatā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the leash to existence is eradicated. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yassatthāya pabbajito, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve attained the goal </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>agārasmānagāriyaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for the sake of which I went forth </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>So me attho anuppatto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>from the lay life to homelessness—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sabbasaṁyojanakkhayo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the ending of all fetters. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Surādho thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
